The function $g(t)$ has the following properties for $t \geq 1$:

(1) $g(t)$ is continuously differentiable;
(2) $g(t)$ is monotone increasing to $\infty$ as $t \to \infty$;
(3) $g'(t)$ is monotone decreasing to 0 as $t \to \infty$;
(4) $tg'(t)$ tends to $\infty$ as $t \to \infty$.

Then the numbers

$$x_n = g(n) - [g(n)], \quad n = 1, 2, 3, \ldots$$

are equidistributed on the interval $[0, 1]$.

The function $w = \frac{2}{i} \arcsin iz$ maps the disk $|z| \leq 1$ onto a finite convex domain which has two corners and lies in the strip

$- \pi \leq \Im w \leq \pi$. Its support function is

$$h(\varphi) = \begin{cases} \cos \varphi \log \left( \sqrt{\cos 2\varphi} + \sqrt{2} \cos \varphi \right)^2 + 2 \sin \varphi \arcsin \left( \sqrt{2} \sin \varphi \right) \\ 0 \leq \varphi \leq \frac{\pi}{4}; \\ \pi \sin \varphi \end{cases}$$

for $0 \leq \varphi \leq \frac{\pi}{4}$;

for $\frac{\pi}{4} \leq \varphi \leq \frac{\pi}{2}$;

$$h(\varphi + \pi) = h(-\varphi) = h(\varphi).$$

